Subject: [PATCH] AMS: discard dead-instance bind timers before persistent restart

A persistent ProcessRecord is reused. Its old soft/hard bind timers must not
ANR the successor before the successor's own startup deadline. Keep provider
cleanup and the new instance's normal startup timeout unchanged.

--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/am/ActivityManagerService.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/am/ActivityManagerService.java
@@ -12694,6 +12694,8 @@ public class ActivityManagerService extends IActivityManager.Stub
             if (index < 0) {
                 ProcessList.remove(pid);
             }
+            mHandler.removeMessages(BIND_APPLICATION_TIMEOUT_SOFT_MSG, app);
+            mHandler.removeMessages(BIND_APPLICATION_TIMEOUT_HARD_MSG, app);
             // Remove provider publish timeout because we will start a new timeout when the
             // restarted process is attaching (if the process contains launching providers).
             mHandler.removeMessages(CONTENT_PROVIDER_PUBLISH_TIMEOUT_MSG, app);
